[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112629,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nasal chondromesenchymal hamartoma (NCMH) is a benign mesenchymal sinonasal tract tumour composed of cysts lined by respiratory epithelium associated with nodules of cartilage and a variably myxoid spindle cell stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112630,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112631,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E90.6 &amp; XH2P15 Benign neoplasm of nasopharynx &amp; Mesenchymal hamartoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112632,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> chondroid hamartoma; nasal hamartoma; congenital mesenchymoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112633,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112634,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Frequently bilateral (~25%), tumours involve the paranasal sinuses (mostly ethmoid) and nasal cavity, sometimes with skull base extension {9537469; 20822816; 26138824}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112635,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Symptoms are nonspecific, with a mass identified {9537469; 16253025; 20822816; 25118636; 26138824}. Patients may have a history of other neoplasms associated with <em>DICER1</em> pathogenic variants {20822816; 24761742; 25118636; 25356068}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Imaging studies show a complex, solid and cystic, heterogeneous soft tissue mass, frequent calcification, and associated bone erosion {9537469; 25117604; 31620849; 31871336}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112636,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fewer than 1% of patients with pleuropulmonary blastoma have NCMH {20822816}. There is a wide age range, but most patients are aged &lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;year (mean: 10&nbsp;years). There is a male predominance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112637,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>NCMH is associated with <em>DICER1</em> pathogenic variants {20822816; 22356457}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112638,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Like other neoplasms in <em>DICER1</em> syndrome, NCMH shows biallelic, loss-of-function, and missense RNase IIIb mutations in <em>DICER1</em>. This combination of mutations is expected to alter expression of microRNAs important in regulating the cell cycle and limiting differentiation {20822816; 24909177; 29343557; 31620849}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112639,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Polypoid, fleshy soft tissue masses</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112640,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>NCMH is composed of epithelial cysts lined by respiratory epithelium associated with nodules of immature to mature cartilage with a rim of spindled cells set in a loose, myxoid to spindled cell stroma. Focal osteoclast-like giant cells may be seen in the stroma near erythrocyte-filled spaces, resembling aneurysmal bone cyst {9537469; 15129948; 16253025; 20822816}. A fibro-osseous proliferation with ossicles or trabeculae of immature (woven) bone can be seen {11231491}. Concurrent sinonasal papilloma and chronic rhinosinusitis may be seen.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The cartilage is highlighted with S100 or SOX9 immunohistochemistry, and SMA highlights stromal myofibroblasts {16253025; 11231491}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes sinonasal tract hamartomas, biphenotypic sinonasal sarcoma, and embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma (which can be seen in <em>DICER1</em> syndrome).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112641,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112642,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>When NCMH is diagnosed, germline <em>DICER1</em> genetic testing is suggested {29343557}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112643,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> cysts lined by respiratory epithelium associated with nodules of immature to mature cartilage within a bland spindled cell stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> biallelic <em>DICER1</em> pathogenic variants in selected cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112644,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 112645,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 26,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Local recurrences may occur with incomplete excision (~25%) {9537469; 26138824; 28385583}. Rare malignant transformation has been reported {23348387}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T11:39:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]